    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d567">

                <pb facs="0786" n="684" xml:id="pg684"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/2625</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-11-11">November 11, 1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Italian Ambassador called this afternoon and left with me the accompanying
                        communication<anchor n="5" xml:id="d567-f1"/> which has just been presented
                    by the Italian Government to all the states members of the League. The
                    Ambassador was also instructed to communicate it to this Government and in doing
                    so expressed the opinion that the same communication was being made to all
                    governments non-members of the League. Signor Rosso translated the communication
                    into French and read it to me. He said that he regarded it as an exceedingly
                    important and very serious communication.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
